# All scripts (private — tooling, scrapers, extractors; data is pre-committed)
# Note: `scripts/*` (not `scripts/`) so per-file re-include rules below work.
# Git refuses to un-ignore files inside a fully-ignored directory.
scripts/*
# CI scripts are public — they run in GitHub Actions and must be tracked
!scripts/ci/
# Unified data-integrity validator — runs in the local gate (npm run
# validate:data / gate:data, see TESTING.md); its check modules and their
# tests must be tracked or new files silently can't be added (existing
# validator files stayed tracked only because they predated this ignore
# rule — a real gap, found 2026-07-10 adding a new test file here).
!scripts/validators/
!scripts/validate-data-integrity.ts

# Role-board CTA gate — runs in the local gate (npm run audit:role-board-ctas)
# and is referenced by a committed package.json script, so it MUST be tracked
# or `npm run audit:role-board-ctas` fails file-not-found for everyone but the
# machine that wrote it. Its .local.test.ts must be tracked for the same reason
# `scripts/validators/` is: otherwise the suite proving the gate can fail is
# invisible to every other checkout. (Found 2026-08-02 the same way the
# validators gap was — the commit silently dropped both files.)
!scripts/audit-role-board-ctas.ts
!scripts/audit-role-board-ctas.local.test.ts

# B+ remediation gates (2026-08-10) — the SAME gap again. All three were wired
# into ci.yml and package.json and all three files were silently dropped by
# `git add`, because `scripts/*` above makes git skip them without a word. The
# branch was green locally (the files exist here) and red in CI with
# ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND, which is the only signal this failure mode ever gives.
# Every future gate under scripts/ needs a line here on the SAME commit that
# adds its ci.yml step.
!scripts/audit-persona-lens.ts
!scripts/audit-changelog-persona-tags.ts
!scripts/audit-migrate-proof-freshness.ts

# The check that stops occurrence five (2026-08-10). Local-only, wired into
# .husky/pre-push rather than ci.yml — a CI step that checks whether CI's files
# are present can only run once they are. Needs its own re-include here for the
# obvious reason.
!scripts/audit-ci-workflow-files.ts

# Role-board coverage gate — the SAME gap, third occurrence (found 2026-08-09
# merging the six-use-cases-per-role work). The 08-09 commit added both the
# ci.yml step and the package.json script but not the file they invoke, because
# `scripts/*` swallowed it: CI would have hard-failed with file-not-found on a
# fresh clone while every local run stayed green. Adding a gate to ci.yml or
# package.json without a matching `!scripts/...` line here is the recurring
# defect — check for one whenever a new scripts/ entry point lands.
!scripts/audit-role-board-coverage.ts

# SBOM version-drift gate — FOURTH occurrence of the trap described directly
# above, and this line exists because the check was written on 2026-08-09,
# `git check-ignore` was run before committing, and it reported the file as
# swallowed. That check is now the habit worth keeping: after adding any
# scripts/ entry point, run
#     git check-ignore -v scripts/<new-file>
# and if it prints a match, add the `!scripts/...` line here BEFORE committing
# the ci.yml or package.json side. Three of the four occurrences shipped.
!scripts/audit-sbom-versions.ts

# Role-board content generator — runs in `npm run build` (npm run generate:
# role-board-content), and personaConfig.ts's live PERSONA_JOURNEY_BOARD
# export now comes from its OUTPUT (src/data/generated/roleBoardContent.
# generated.ts, not scripts/-ignored — see the entry for that path below).
# Same failure mode as the CTA gate two entries up if left ignored: every
# checkout but the one that wrote it gets file-not-found. `lib/` holds the
# token registry both this script and any future role-board tooling shares.
!scripts/generate-role-board-content.ts
!scripts/lib/
!scripts/lib/roleBoardTokens.ts

# Role-board content maintenance aid — npm run audit:role-board-content,
# backing the audit-role-board-content skill. Same reason: referenced by a
# committed package.json script.
!scripts/audit-role-board-content.ts

# Data-filename generator — runs in `npm run build` and `predev`
# (npm run generate:data-filenames) and emits src/data/generated/
# dataFilenames.generated.ts, which useVersionStore.ts imports. Same trap as
# every entry above: `scripts/*` makes `git add` a silent no-op, and without
# this line the build fails file-not-found in CI and every other checkout
# while staying green on the machine that wrote it.
!scripts/generate-data-filenames.ts

# NVD CVE scraper — runs weekly in .github/workflows/update-cve.yml (public
# CI), must be tracked or that workflow fails with "No such file or directory"
# (as it silently did for weeks — see git history). Reads public CPE xref CSV,
# calls the public NVD API, writes public cve-snapshot.json: nothing private.
# Weekly-cron CI scripts — invoked on GitHub runners by
# .github/workflows/trusted-source-freshness.yml and update-protocol-matrix.yml;
# must be tracked or those workflows fail file-not-found (the scrape-nvd.py
# failure mode above). Sanitized ports: public inputs (trusted_sources CSV,
# pqcProtocolMatrix.ts, IETF datatracker), public outputs. No LLM phase.
!scripts/enrich-protocol-matrix.py
!scripts/apply-protocol-matrix-updates.ts
# Its unit tests — the downgrade guard (F8, 2026-07-25) is the reason this
# script needs any. scripts/* is ignored wholesale, so every tracked file
# here needs its own negation; without this line the tests exist locally and
# nowhere else, which is exactly the failure mode the guard protects against.
!scripts/apply-protocol-matrix-updates.test.ts
# Build-pipeline generators are public — `npm run build` invokes them to
# produce OSCAL + CBOM JSON from committed CSV data. Reading public input,
# emitting public output: nothing private to protect.
!scripts/generate-oscal.ts
!scripts/generate-cbom.ts
# Derives algorithmProperties.ts from the committed algorithm reference CSV;
# CI-relevant --check mode. Public input, public output.
!scripts/generate-algorithm-properties.ts
# SEO build steps — `npm run build` invokes both: generate-sitemap emits
# public/sitemap.xml, and prerender writes per-route static HTML into dist/.
# Read public routeMeta, emit public output: nothing private to protect.
!scripts/generate-sitemap.ts
!scripts/prerender.ts
# Simulation activity-tree generator — emits the committed dated trees in
# src/simulation/trees from the public framework + hub registries.
!scripts/gen-sim-trees.mjs
# Timeline single-source codegen — derives sim/page facts from the timeline CSV.
# Tracked: runs in prebuild and the CI freshness gate.
!scripts/gen-timeline-facts.mjs
# Simulation live-feed generator — emits the committed dated sim_feed_*.csv.
!scripts/gen-sim-feed.mjs

# Workshop flow static audit — runs in CI, must be tracked. Reads
# public/workshop/*.json + src/. The companion timing fixer
# (scripts/fix-workshop-caption-timing.ts) stays private since it mutates
# authored content.
!scripts/audit-workshop-flows.ts

# Reference-cache drift audit — runs in the reference-cache-drift CI
# workflow weekly. Reads public/{library,timeline,threats}/manifest.json,
# re-fetches each entry, compares SHA-256 against the stored hash. Pure
# read-only inputs, public report output — nothing private to protect.
!scripts/audit-reference-cache-drift.ts
!scripts/audit-reference-cache-drift.test.ts

# Migration-phases hygiene gate — runs in ci.yml (npm run audit:migration-phases,
# also part of gate:data). The .ts was tracked only because it predated the
# `scripts/*` rule and had no re-include of its own; its test could not be added
# at all until 2026-07-29, which is exactly the silent gap the validators comment
# above describes. Both are listed now so neither can be lost on a re-add.
# Reads the public product catalog CSV, writes nothing — nothing private.
!scripts/audit-migration-phases.ts
!scripts/audit-migration-phases.local.test.ts

# RAG index freshness report — regenerated each run by the scheduled
# rag-index-freshness workflow (uploaded as a build artifact, not committed).
public/data/rag-index-freshness.json

# Matrix prose-doc-ID audit — CI gate that guards `src/data/pqcProtocolMatrix.ts`
# against doc-ID citations leaking into note / deploymentNote / playground /
# liveDeployment text fields. Pure read-only against public data.
!scripts/audit-matrix-refs.ts
# Jurisdiction-refs gate — CI check that all jurisdiction data consumers import
# from the canonical CSV-driven source (jurisdictionsData.ts).
!scripts/audit-jurisdiction-refs.ts

# Sandbox scenario sync generator — CI gate (sync:sandbox:check) that keeps
# src/data/sandboxScenarios.ts regenerated from the public sandbox source repo
# (pqctoday-sandbox/ui/src/data/scenarios.ts). Pure read-only against public
# data; must be tracked so CI and other devs can run `npm run sync:sandbox`.
!scripts/sync-sandbox-scenarios.ts

# Module infographic coverage audit — CI gate that fails the build if any
# MODULE_CATALOG entry lacks public/images/infographics/pqcstd_<id>.png.
# CuriousSummaryBanner has no fallback chain; missing PNG = broken image.
!scripts/audit-module-infographics.ts

# Content revision-coverage audit (LEARN-MODULE-REVISION-HISTORY-REMEDIATION-
# PLAN-07312026.md Phase 2, covers Learn modules + Playground tools) — CI
# gate, `npm run audit:content-revision-coverage`.
!scripts/audit-content-revision-coverage.ts

# Learn-module snapshot exporter — emits the JSON snapshot the maintainer
# agent's Python validators consume (learn-modules maintenance Phase 0).
# Execute-imports real manifests + AST-extracts content.ts/component text:
# public inputs, JSON output written outside the repo. Must be tracked so
# `npm run export:learn-snapshot` works from a fresh checkout.
!scripts/export-learn-manifest-snapshot.ts

# Timeline country-alias audit — CI gate that validates countryAliases.ts
# against the latest Timeline CSV. Pure read-only against public data.
!scripts/audit-timeline-aliases.ts

# Parallel-session worktree helper — developer tooling, no crypto or data
# secrets. Documented in CLAUDE.md ("Parallel sessions: use git worktrees").
!scripts/new-worktree.sh
!scripts/refresh-index.sh

# Compliance country-token audit — runs in CI. Validates every country/region
# token in the latest compliance CSV resolves through COUNTRY_CODE_TO_NAME and
# COUNTRY_TO_REGION in src/data/complianceData.ts. Pure read-only.
!scripts/audit-compliance-countries.ts

# Semantic-token audit — CI gate that scans src/ for hardcoded Tailwind palette
# classes that violate ux-standard.md §S1.2. Pure read-only against public src.
!scripts/audit-semantic-tokens.ts

# Timeline electronic-evidence pipeline — mirrors the threats-evidence pattern.
# Downloads SourceUrl content per active CSV row to public/timeline/ and emits
# public/timeline/evidence/manifest.json so the Gantt popover can prove its
# claims are backed by on-disk documents. Audit script is the CI gate.
#
# 2026-08-09: the two snapshotters (wayback-snapshot-timeline.ts,
# snapshot-timeline-via-playwright.ts) were REMOVED from this list and deleted
# here — scrapers live in pqctoday-priv, which already held byte-identical
# copies of both. Nothing referenced them: no npm script, no CI step, no test.
# The rest of the pipeline stays public for now because the hub copies of
# download-timeline-evidence.ts and enrich-protocol-matrix.py are AHEAD of
# pqctoday-priv's (by 22 and 305 lines), so moving them means syncing content
# first, not deleting. audit-timeline-evidence.ts must stay public regardless —
# CI runs it.
!scripts/audit-timeline-evidence.ts
!scripts/sync-timeline-csv-from-manifest.ts
!scripts/audit-timeline-enrichment-freshness.ts

# Content-freshness audit — CI gate that flags time-sensitive sim claims
# (CMVP/FIPS status, protocol-matrix snapshot, Q-Day anchor) aged past 90 days.
# Reads src/data/contentFreshness.ts. Must be tracked to run in CI.
!scripts/audit-content-freshness.ts

# Module review-freshness gate (WS22 Stage 4) — the absolute-age half of
# audit:content-freshness, which is already whitelisted above. Same
# `scripts/*` trap: without these two lines `git add` is a silent no-op, the
# gate's own helper never leaves the machine that wrote it, and
# audit-content-freshness.ts fails module-not-found in CI and every other
# checkout while staying green locally.
!scripts/moduleReviewFreshness.ts
!scripts/audit-content-freshness.local.test.ts

# Vendor-ref integrity audit — CI gate that validates vendor_id assignments in
# the product catalog against the vendor roadmap CSV. Catches wrong VND-*
# assignments (deprecated refs, name mismatches). Pure read-only against public data.
!scripts/audit-vendor-refs.ts
# Proof-gate: every curated leader row's KeyResourceRefs must resolve to a
# real, non-deprecated library reference_id. Pure read-only against public data.
!scripts/audit-leaders-refs.ts
# CSV-archival gate: every dated-CSV loader eager-globs its whole prefix into
# the JS bundle, so un-archived old revisions silently bloat the production
# build (broke it outright on 2026-07-26). Pure read-only against src/data/.
!scripts/audit-csv-archival.ts
!scripts/audit-csv-archival.test.ts

# CSV copy-forward gate: dated generations are different FILENAMES, so two
# sessions each writing one merge cleanly with no conflict while the loader
# serves only the newest — rows present in one and absent from the other just
# disappear, with no conflict, error or failing test. Runs in the local gate
# (npm run audit:csv-copy-forward, wired into .husky/pre-push).
# The .test.ts line is not decoration: `scripts/*` above made `git add` a
# silent no-op for it, so the tests were written, passed, and were left out of
# the commit that added them. Same failure this file already records for the
# validators (2026-07-10) and the role-board gates.
!scripts/audit-csv-copy-forward.ts
!scripts/audit-csv-copy-forward.test.ts

# Publication-date gate: library.initial_publication_date, timeline.SourceDate
# and vendor-roadmaps.publish_date all mean "the source document's own
# publication date" — add_row.py used to fill them with the ingest timestamp
# instead, undetected, until the 2026-08-11 remediation. Blocks a future date
# and an unexplained same-day cluster (the shape an ingest batch makes).
!scripts/audit-publication-dates.ts

# Merge-all coverage gate: the sibling failure mode to the above — a loader
# that MERGES every dated file (not "newest wins") silently loses a document
# the moment it's archived out of a directory the loader's glob doesn't cover.
# Broke the CSWP.39 maturity corpus for 12 days starting 2026-07-26; see
# archive-sweep-audit-08072026.md. Pure read-only against src/data/ + the
# registered loader source files.
!scripts/audit-merge-all-coverage.ts
!scripts/audit-merge-all-coverage.test.ts

